      \includegraphics[width=0.27\textwidth]{figures/fig1.png}
      \caption{Example of the state-space cooperative game model, described by a spanning set including two vectors with the fixed state $s$. The red and blue arrowed lines are two games, such as $v$ and $w$, whose difference is measured by the $\theta$. The shading area indicates the spectrum of generated cooperative games for $k_{C} \geq 0$ and $\sum k_{C} = 1$, which occupies the first quadrant.}
