\paragraph{Computation.}
We define a \textit{computation} as a unit of work composed of one or more instructions, where exactly one of the instructions is a write of a scalar value to a data container.

\paragraph{Loop.}
A \textit{loop} comprises an iterator with its initial values and update criterion, a termination condition, and a loop body composed of a sequence of computations. 

