%     In a stochastic game, a joint policy $\bm{\mu}^*=(\mu^*_1,\cdots,\mu^*_N) \in \mathcal{U}$ is a local Nash equilibrium if there exists $\epsilon>0$ such that for any agent $i$ and policy $\mu_i\in \mathcal{U}_i\setminus \{\mu_i^*\} :\|\mu_i-\mu_i^*\|\le \epsilon$, we have
