\subsection{Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning}\label{sec:exp_MARL}

In this section, we first test our MV-MATRPO algorithm in Scenario 1 of Section~\ref{sec:exp_model based} to compare its results with those of MV-MAPI and demonstrate its validity. Second, we evaluate the effectiveness of MV-MATRPO in a larger-scale MMS comprising five microgrids, each equipped with a renewable energy generator, a demand load unit, and a storage unit.

We construct simulated environments for the two scenarios, where the power of renewable energy generators and the demand load units of each microgrid follow the transition probability matrices $P_g$ and $P_d$, respectively. At each time step $t$, each microgrid takes action $a_{i,t}$ based on its current policy $\mu_i$ and state $s_t$. The next state $s_{t+1}$  is then received by each microgrid from simulated environments. As shown in Algorithm~\ref{alg:MVTRPO}, trajectory data are collected repeatedly through the interactions of all microgrids with the simulated environment. The policies of all microgrids are updated iteratively based on these data. The parameters of Algorithm~\ref{alg:MVTRPO} are provided in Appendix~\ref{sec:appd_hyperparameter}. 

We validate the algorithm in the two scenarios with different coefficients $\beta$. In all experiments, the initial policies and update orders are generated randomly. The experimental results are presented in Figure~\ref{fig:tracurve-mg3} and Figure~\ref{fig:tracurve-mg5}, where each training curve is averaged over six random seeds and shaded by the standard deviation. 

