We use an LLM to encode each table column into a vector. For adaption to the given table set, we fine-tune the LLM using a self-supervsed contrastive learning algorithm called SwAV ({\bf Sw}apped {\bf A}ssignments between multiple {\bf V}iews) which was originally proposed for image embedding and clustering, and has been successfully applied over different kinds of data \cite{DBLP:conf/nips/CaronMMGBJ20}.
