The approach involves two steps: (i) identifying the subject column of each table using an existing technique proposed in \cite{DBLP:journals/semweb/Zhang17}; and (ii) clustering the tables based on the semantic similarity of the embeddings of their subject columns, where the number of clusters is chosen with the Silhouette Coefficient \cite{DBLP:journals/silhouette}. 

