\section{Conclusion}

In this study, we implemented a method for forecasting storm trajectories over continuous 6-hour intervals using a Transformer model combined with a grid-based coordinate mapping system. The model successfully predicted storm paths for the next 6 hours, achieving an accuracy of 0.783 and a mean squared error (MSE) of 0.0086. When compared with NOAA methods and GPRA benchmarks, our model demonstrated superior performance while also completing training more quickly.

