Compute-bound kernels, such as matrix multiplication (Case 2), Jacobi 2D (Cases 6 and 12), and conjugate gradient (Case 14), scaled efficiently, achieving speedups of up to nearly 8×. For example, Jacobi 2D (Case 6) reduced runtime from 7.82 to 1.36 seconds—a 5.7× improvement.

