\noindent Observe that the right-hand side of \Cref{eq:gammanystrom} is the \Nystrom{} approximation of $K_\gamma$, which is exact on the principal submatrix corresponding to the subset of indices $\I$. After considering the diagonal similarity transformation relating $\ObliqueP_{\I,\Kill}(t)$ to $\NonSymObliqueP_{\I,\Kill}(t)$, we arrive at a key interpretation of the structure-preserving dynamics: for any killing rate $\gamma>0$ and any initialization, the integrated occupation time in each of the selected states $i \in \I$ exactly matches that of the original dynamics. Note that we must consider a positive killing rate in order for the integrated occupation time to be finite.

