    \end{eqn}
    so in particular $ \Norms{I_2 (\gamma)} \ra 0 $ as $\gamma \ra 0$.

    Thus we can ignore $I_2$ asymptotically, and we turn our attention to $I_1$. First we focus on the contribution due to the vertical crossbar $\mathcal{C}_2 (T)$ as defined in the proof of \Cref{th:dissipative}, cf. \Cref{eq:contourdef0}.
