    Moreover $1/\vert z\vert^2 = O(T^{-2})$ for $z \in \mathcal{C}_{2B} (T)$, and by \Cref{th:recurrent-obliqueness} we know that $\Obs^\Kill$ are convergent as $\gamma \ra 0$. Therefore from \Cref{th:resolvent-obliqueness}, it follows that $\Norms{\ObliqueRes^\Kill(z) - \OrthRes^\Kill(z)} = O( \vert \im (z) \vert^{-2})$ on $\mathcal{C}_2 (T) $. Then by the same reasoning \Cref{eq:C2Bint} as in the proof of \Cref{th:dissipative}, the $\mathcal{C}_{2B}$ contribution is $O(1/\sqrt{T})$ and in particular vanishes in our limit $\gamma \ra 0$.

