We will also use the celebrated bound on the DPP expectation \cite{Chen2022-randomly,Guruswami2012-optimal,Belabbas2009-spectral,Derezinski2021-determinantal}:
\begin{eqn} \label{eq:dpp-nystrom}
    \DPPfunction_k(M) \leq \lrp{1 + \frac{r}{k-r+1}} (\Tr[M] - \Tr^{(r)}[M]), 
\end{eqn}
in which $\Tr^{(r)}[M]$ denote the sum of the largest $r$ eigenvalues.


