            &\stackrel{\re}{\leftrightarrow}\angel{(\alpha^d)^{-d}}{\angel{(\beta^d)^{-d}}{(P\land Q)}} \lor \angel{\alpha^d}{\angel{\beta^d}{Q}}\\
            &\stackrel{\dA}{\mathmakebox[\widthof{$\stackrel{\re}{\leftrightarrow}$}]{\leftrightarrow}} \angel{\alpha^{-d}}{\angel{\beta^{-d}}{(P\land Q)}} \lor \demon{\alpha}{\demon{\beta}{Q}}
        \end{aligned}
        \]
        Using the dual rule, Demon's modality is converted into Angel's modality. Then, the rule $\re$ that has been proven earlier, can be used. Then the dual rule is applied to convert the result back. This yields the right-hand side of the equivalence, so the claim is proved.

        The admissibility proof for both Emergency rules is done by induction over the complexity of the game $\alpha$.

