                &\angel{\alpha^{-d}}{(P\land Q)} \lor \angel{\alpha}{P})\\ 
                &\land (\angel{\alpha^{-d}}{(P\land Q)} \lor \demon{\alpha}{Q})
            \end{aligned}\\
            &\stackrel{\text{prop. L.}}{\mathmakebox[\widthof{$\stackrel{\text{C.A. 1, 2}}{\leftrightarrow}$}]{\leftrightarrow}} \angel{\alpha^{-d}}{(P\land Q)} \lor (\angel{\alpha}{P} \land \demon{\alpha}{Q})\\
            &\stackrel{\id}{\mathmakebox[\widthof{$\stackrel{\text{C.A. 1, 2}}{\leftrightarrow}$}]{\leftrightarrow}} \angel{\alpha^{-d}}{(P\land Q)}
        \end{aligned}\]
        The proof for $\AD$ can be easily done by using both complementarization axioms on the left-hand side of the equivalence. Then, $\angel{\alpha^{-d}}{(P\land Q)}$ is factored out. Afterwards, the rule $\id$ can be applied, yielding the right-hand side of the equivalence.
